        "设备参数",
        "容量"
      ],
      "guide": "references/facts-device.md",
      "source": "library/ascriptor/devices/profiles/950.json",
      "case": null,
      "device": "a5",
      "note": "Read the ratio, not the counts: two vector sub-blocks per cube core holds on all seven shipped profiles, while the counts differ between the part `ascriptor.a5` names and a 950PR card. `block_dim` comes from the profile, never from a literal."
    },
    {
      "id": "sparse-mask",
      "terms": [
        "sparse",
        "sparse mask",
        "top-k mask",
        "data-dependent mask",
        "runtime mask",
        "presence table",
        "gather mask",
        "scatter mask",
        "epoch marker",
        "稀疏",
        "稀疏掩码",
        "运行时掩码",
        "数据决定的掩码",
        "presence 表",
        "代号标记"
      ],
      "guide": "references/patterns.md",
      "source": "kernels/ascriptor_kernels/attention/a5_presence_mask",
      "api_guide": "library/docs/api/mask-write-semantics.md",
      "note": "The decision first, the mechanics second. Keeping a data-dependent mask as ordinary numbers and rebuilding the predicate costs 32 times the bytes of a packed predicate, and is still the better trade because the table then covers a chunk and is rebuilt: vector arithmetic is cheap next to UB capacity here. The backend can spill a predicate (`vf.mask_to_ub` and `vf.ub_to_mask` both print), so do not record the operator surface as the reason. Then three mechanics in one file: generation markers replacing the clear, one unsigned test feeding `reg_to_ub_scatter(mask=)`, and a masked `expsub` whose zeroed lanes are the masking. The row-selection half of a sparse contract is a different route with its own owner: `api.indexed_row_gather` covers gathering rows by index, and the attention combinations of the two - causal geometry, GQA sharing, `Dv<Dk` column blocking - have no unit at all. This unit rebuilds a dense predicate; it does not move rows.",
      "device": "a5"
    },
    {
      "id": "indexed-row-gather",
      "terms": [
        "indexed row gather",
        "row gather",
        "gather rows",
        "gather by index",
        "index gather",
        "kv row gather",
        "gather kv rows",
        "topk gather",
        "top-k gather",
        "sparse attention gather",
        "sparse attention row gather",
        "sparse row selection",
        "按索引 gather",
        "按索引 gather KV 行",
        "索引 gather",
        "KV 行 gather",
        "按索引搬行",
        "按索引取行",
        "稀疏 gather",
        "稀疏注意力 gather",
        "topk 索引 gather"
      ],
      "guide": "references/attention-authoring.md",
      "source": "library/examples/api/indexed_row_gather",
      "api_guide": "library/docs/api/storage.md",
      "note": "This is the transfer, and only the transfer. A contract that supplies its KV rows as indices changes how the tile is assembled and nothing in the attention mathematics, so read it for three decisions and then leave: each table is gathered at its own row width, and the two outcomes of the wrong width differ - separately declared tables reject it, a `Dv` prefix of a `Dk`-wide row accepts it silently and returns the next field; the copies are unconditional, so a slot padded up to the tile height still has to name a legal row and it is the mask that discards it; and a clamped destination row stays inside the tensor while overwriting the last real row, so the guard before the store is the answer. The attention combinations this route belongs to have no unit - see the page's uncovered list before assuming otherwise. Cost: one gathered row is one transfer descriptor.",
      "case": null,
      "device": "a5"
    },
    {
      "id": "cross-side-handoff",
      "terms": [
        "cross-side handoff",
        "cross side handoff",
        "handoff",
        "handshake",
        "mutex",
        "VcMutex",
        "CvMutex",
        "lock",
        "ready",
        "wait",
        "free",
        "credit",
        "credits",
        "publish a tile",
        "hand a tile over",
        "跨侧交接",
        "跨侧握手",
        "握手",
        "互斥",
        "信用",
        "发布 tile",
        "交接"
      ],
      "guide": "references/cross-side-handoff.md",
      "source": "library/examples/api/cube_vector_roundtrip",
      "api_guide": "library/docs/api/synchronization.md",
      "case": null,
      "device": "a5",
      "note": "The four calls first, the credit count second. `lock`/`ready` belong to the producing side and `wait`/`free` to the consuming one, and every read of the handed-over buffer belongs between `wait` and `free` - a `wait` followed straight by `free` returns the slot before anything read it, and the credits still balance, so a hazard prover can stay silent. Only then does `depth` matter, and `guards=` is the spelling that cannot drift from the buffer."
    }
  ],
